      RED SKY INTERACTIVE 1998 DEMO CD B E F O R E    R U N N I N G    T H E    D E M O      1. Make sure the monitor is set to 256 colors:          - Open the System Folder.          - Open the Control Panels Folder.          - Double-click the Monitors control panel.          - Select 256 Colors from the 'Settings of selected monitor' list.          - Click the 'Options...' button.          - Select 640 x 480 from the 'Select a monitor setting' list.           - Click OK.          - Select 'Rearrange On Close' and close the Monitors control panel.      2. Quit any other open applications.      3. To run the demo, double-click on 'Red Sky 98' in the CD window.D E M O    N A V I G A T I O N     When launched, the demo starts by displaying a black splash screen with the RSI logo. At this point, you can simply click the logo to start the Entertainment module, or Shift-click to go directly to the Work Module.     Once you have entered the first module, you can use the following navigation commands at any time:     Control-E\tab Go to Entertainment Module     Control-W\tab Go to Work Module      Control-X\tab Go to Exit Module     Control-Q\tab Quit immediately     Additionally, each module provides navigation buttons to navigate directly by using the mouse.     When viewing the assets contained in the Work Module, you can press RETURN  to go  back to the Work Module's main menu.     Please note that once you have gone to the Exit Module, you can no longer return to any other module. After the exit sequence is completed, the program will automatically quit.     Spacebar Shortcuts:     In the Entertainment module, you can press the spacebar through the introductory screens to reach the actual presentation more quickly.     In the Exit Module, you can press the spacebar to cut straight from the cowboy exit animation to the credits roll, and press the spacebar (several times) during the credits roll to quit immediately.